{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 150, :comments ["<b>They have drawn near</b> — These are pursuers of lust who have distanced themselves from knowledge of Your Torah. Scripture records upon it the punishment of Adam and Cain and the men of the Flood and the Tower and Pharaoh. And to say 'they have drawn near' of a people who 'have disticated [their] way' is exceedingly renowned in the Songs."], :book :psalms, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 119, :notes {0 "The phrase 'דרך בשירים נכבדת מאד' is obscure; read hyper-literally. 'רחקו דרך' likely alludes to the next verse's רחקו ממך רעים. The reference of 'בשירים' (in the Songs/Psalms) is unclear and may be textually difficult."}, :source-witnesses [["Ibn Ezra on Psalms -- Daat" "http://www.daat.ac.il/he-il/tanach/parshanut_hamikra/full-text/eben-ezra/tehilim"] ["Wikisource Mikraot Gedolot" "http://en.wikisource.org/wiki/Mikraot_Gedolot/"] ["Tanakh, Venice, 1617-1619" "https://dlib.rsl.ru/viewer/01007514045#?page=4"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T19:40:57.763182004Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}